This is Claude desktop not claude.ai

The current claude_desktop_config.json has:

{
  "preferences": {
    "launchEnabled": false,
    "launchPreviewPersistSession": true,
    "launchPreviewPersistedWorkspaces": [
      "ec6f037f5029"
    ],
    "coworkScheduledTasksEnabled": true,
    "sidebarMode": "chat",
    "bypassPermissionsModeEnabled": true,
    "coworkWebSearchEnabled": true
  }
}

I don't want to lose preferences or settings or break my current setup, what do I replace it with now?

Merge the `mcpServers` key into your existing file. Replace the entire file contents with this:

```json
{
  "preferences": {
    "launchEnabled": false,
    "launchPreviewPersistSession": true,
    "launchPreviewPersistedWorkspaces": [
      "ec6f037f5029"
    ],
    "coworkScheduledTasksEnabled": true,
    "sidebarMode": "chat",
    "bypassPermissionsModeEnabled": true,
    "coworkWebSearchEnabled": true
  },
  "mcpServers": {
    "filesystem": {
      "command": "npx.cmd",
      "args": [
        "-y",
        "[redacted:social-handle]/server-filesystem",
        "[redacted:local-path] Infinite Labyrinth"
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

All your preferences stay intact — I just added the `mcpServers` block as a sibling key. Using `npx.cmd` instead of `npx` since you're on Windows.

After saving, fully quit Claude Desktop (right-click the system tray icon → **Quit**, not just X the window), then relaunch. Look for the hammer icon (🔨) at the bottom of the input box.

**One thing to flag:** Even once the MCP server is running, this current conversation won't pick up the new tools — they're registered when a conversation starts. You'll need to **start a new conversation** after the restart for the filesystem tools to be available. We can continue this design work there, or you can link me back to this chat's context.
